# Testing requirements

For contribution tickets with `type: bug`, satisfy every item in `bug_fix_requirements` from `contrib-runway/policies/n8n.yaml`.
A requirement may be waived only when the policy allows waivers and the ticket
contains:

- The specific waived requirement
- A written justification
- An approving owner
- An approval reference

Simulation tickets do not automatically waive testing requirements.

Typical requirements:

- `linked_or_approved_issue` — ticket references an approved/linked issue (simulation tickets count when `simulation: true` and status is approved).
- `regression_test` — add or extend an automated test that fails on the old behavior and passes on the fix.
- `valid_behavior_test` — keep or add coverage that valid inputs still behave correctly.
- `manual_test_instructions` — document short manual steps under `contrib-runway/evidence/` or in the PR description when asked.

## Where to put tests

- Prefer colocated tests next to the changed node/module (Vitest in this repo).
- Run the smallest relevant test command from the repository root, for example: `pnpm --filter n8n-nodes-base test -- nodes/DateTime/test/node/DateTime.test.ts`
- Also run the package's typecheck and lint commands before claiming review readiness.
- Mock external I/O; do not hit real network services.

## Do not claim READY evidence without tests

If the policy requires a regression test, a code-only change without a test is incomplete — even when `check.ts` returned READY for approval/area.
